<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 18.72 pct in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 18.72 pct in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	18.72	    -53	     18.49     18.90</p>
<p>91-Day	19.67	    - 8	     19.57     19.73</p>
<p>182-Day     20.63	    -35	     20.57     20.68</p>
<p>343-Day     20.83				20.71     20.89</p>
<p>Last week the 350-day paper was assigned at 20.94 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   2.23 bln pesos    2.79</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   3.10 bln pesos    3.88</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   3.07 bln pesos    3.84</p>
<p>343-Day     600 million pesos   1.68 bln pesos    2.80</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.36 on demand of 10.08 billion pesos compared with 4.90 the week before on demand of 14.71 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   18 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    6 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			   5 basis points</p>
<p>    343-Day			   6 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
</text>
